    "Aggregate local simulations only. No live tournament results, account data, or hand histories are included.",
    "The independent sampling unit is a table; intervals are unadjusted 95% intervals.",
    "Mean-points intervals use mean +/- 1.95996398454 times sample SD / sqrt(number of tables).",
    "Win and finish-rate intervals use the Wilson binomial formula.",
    "Points come from the official scoring function, including tied-bust payout sharing and ICM at the hand cap; they are not inferred from finish counts.",
    "Tied finishing ranks can cause more than three entries to have rank <=3. Top-three rank is not a count of distinct paid slots.",
    "Repeated default bots within one table are not independent observations; the effective sample size for the hero is 200 tables per scenario.",
    "The passive scenario has a degenerate empirical mean interval because every observed score was 50. Its 200/200 wins do not prove a guaranteed 100% win rate.",
    "These fixed, weak reference-bot fields do not predict performance against the unknown live tournament field.",
